# Tree / layout conventions

Twin prose: `maintainer/agents/tree.md`.

## Prefer this shape

```text
net/portswigger/mcp/<domain>/
  Foo.kt              # one concern per file
  Bar.kt
```

- **Major domains** get a package once a file grows fat or gains a second concern (`repeater/`, `tools/repeater/`, future `ui/`).
- **Naming:** folders match concepts (`security`, `schema`, `config`) — avoid catch-all `util` unless truly generic.

## Where code lives

| Kind | Package / path |
|------|----------------|
| MCP registration helpers | `tools/McpTool.kt` |
| Tool handlers | `tools/` (split by domain over time) |
| `@Serializable` MCP / JSON DTOs | `schema/` or domain (e.g. `repeater/RepeaterTabModels.kt`) |
| Montoya + approvals | `security/` |
| Burp MCP tab UI | `config/` |
| Swing Repeater discovery | `repeater/` → shared `ui/` |
| Ktor SSE | `KtorServerManager.kt` |
| Tests | `src/test/kotlin/...` same package as main |

## Rules

- Logic modules **import** DTOs; do not duplicate serializable types.
- **Do not** put Swing tree walking inside tool handler bodies — call discovery layer.
- Split **`Tools.kt`** into domain registration files when touching many tools ([`maintainer/phases/refactor.md`](maintainer/phases/refactor.md)).
- Constants (error strings, UI labels, timeouts): colocate until `shared/constants/` exists, then move.

## File size

Prefer several focused files over a 400+ line god file.

## Gradle

- `./gradlew test` — required gate
- Dependencies: `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
- Stdio proxy: `./gradlew fetchProxyJar` → `build/proxy/mcp-proxy-all.jar` (not `libs/`)
